.TH QFW-SITE-SERVICES 8 "September 2026" "QFw Slurm Cluster" "Administration"
.SH NAME
qfw-site-services \- manage the virtual cluster QFw service plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-site-services
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]
.RB [ \-\-target " " target ]
.BR start | status | stop | restart | recover
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-site-services
starts and stops the administrator-owned site directory, NWQSim DVM and QPM,
and IQM QPM used by the QFw virtual Slurm cluster.
The command runs on
.B slurmctld
as root and invokes the installed QFw service managers on their assigned
service nodes.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B start
Start the selected target.  The default
.B all
target starts the directory service, NWQSim service, and IQM service in
dependency order.  Partial aggregate startup failure removes only components
created by that invocation.  Starting a QPM target requires a ready directory
service.
.TP
.B status
Report the state of each service manager and the gateway endpoint.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the selected target.  The default aggregate action stops the IQM QPM,
NWQSim QPM and DVM, then the directory service.  A targeted directory stop is
rejected while a managed QPM remains ready.
.TP
.B restart
Stop and then start the selected target.  A stop failure prevents startup.
.TP
.B recover
Attempt to stop the selected target, tolerate stale or already-stopped state,
and then start it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-target " target"
Select
.BR all ,
.BR directory ,
.BR nwqsim ,
or
.BR iqm .
The default is
.BR all .
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print the remote commands and dependency order without executing them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The command accepts administrator overrides through
.BR QFW_INSTALL_PREFIX ,
.BR QFW_VENV ,
.BR QFW_SHARED_ROOT ,
.BR QFW_SITE_CONFIG ,
.BR QFW_SITE_RUN_ROOT ,
.BR QFW_DIR_NODE ,
.BR QFW_NWQSIM_NODE ,
.BR QFW_IQM_NODE ,
.BR QFW_SIMULATOR_NODES ,
.BR QFW_GATEWAY_HOST ,
.BR QFW_GATEWAY_PORT ,
and
.BR QFW_SITE_START_TIMEOUT .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/openqse/qfw/site.yaml
Default QFw site configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/qfw-site-services
Default administrator-owned manager state root on each service host.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
qfw-site-services start
qfw-site-services status --target nwqsim
qfw-site-services recover --target iqm
qfw-site-services stop --target all
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The command requires root for live actions.  It passes protected configuration
paths to the QPM and does not display or replace credential contents.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1),
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
.BR qfw-sinfo (1),
.BR qfw-squeue (1)
